{
 "method": {
  "summary": "Worked by an implementation that does not import this library, in exact decimals, then rounded only here. The member is invented: no figure belongs to anybody.",
  "payPath": "Today's pay on the member's Agenda for Change ladder while steps remain, then GAD's promotional index (the two non-manual columns averaged, linear between the printed five-year rows) forwards from the top step and backwards from today, read at the age whose birthday falls in each scheme year. Index as printed on page 3 of the GAD 2020 valuation assumptions summary (docs/source-archive.md, SA-57).",
  "section1995": "Membership in whole scheme years (every window here starts on 1 April and ends on 31 March) from 1 April 2004, to 31 March 2015 or, on the legacy basis, to 31 March 2022; over 80, times the best single year's pay of the last three to the scheme year of leaving. Automatic lump sum three times the pension. Before 60, factors from tables 1-401 (pension) and 1-407 (lump sum), keyed by age in complete years and months; from 60, no factor.",
  "section2015": "Career average in today's money: 1/54 of each scheme year's pay, the pot revalued 1.5% a year while in service, from 2022-23 to the scheme year of leaving. On the 2015 basis the remedy window is the same walk over 2015-16 to 2021-22, carried at 1.5% a year to the scheme year of leaving. Factor from table 0-420 before the pension age of 68 (part months rounded up) or 0-421 after it (rounded down).",
  "factorTables": "Read from the text of the NHSBSA Early and Late Retirement Factors extract (docs/source-archive.md, SA-02), a separate reading from both the library's transcriptions in src/gad/ and the mirror CSVs in this directory.",
  "cash": "Maximum cash is (60P + 5A) / 14, the scheme's quarter of capital value at 20:1 with \u00a312 of cash for each \u00a31 of pension given up; the Lump Sum Allowance does not bind at any of these drawings and is not applied. The pension left is P less (cash less A) / 12."
 },
